{"slug": "dcs-control-modes-manual-auto-cascade", "question": "What Are the Control Modes in a DCS?", "body_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">DCS control modes are the operating states of a PID block that decide who writes its setpoint and who writes its output:</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0 4px;font-size:16px;\"><tr style=\"background:#1a2b4a;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Mode</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Setpoint From</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Output From</th></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">MAN</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Operator, often tracking PV</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Operator</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">AUTO</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Operator</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">PID algorithm</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">CAS</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Upstream block</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">PID algorithm</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">RCAS</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">External host</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">PID algorithm</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">ROUT</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Not used</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">External program</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">OOS</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Not used</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Holds last value</td></tr></table><p style=\"margin:0;\">Bumpless transfer and PV tracking stop the output jumping when modes change.</p>"}